WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.360 --> 00:00:03.300
They're titans of the comic book movie world — but&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:03.300 --> 00:00:07.320
are Kevin Feige and James Gunn&nbsp;
destined to be friends… or foes?

00:00:07.320 --> 00:00:11.880
DC shocked Hollywood when they announced that&nbsp;
James Gunn and Peter Safran had been tapped to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:11.880 --> 00:00:17.700
lead DC Studios, overseeing film, television,&nbsp;
and animation for the comic book giant. Gunn,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:17.700 --> 00:00:21.180
being one of the few people to have&nbsp;
worked with both Marvel and DC,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:21.180 --> 00:00:25.380
is revered by comic fans for his&nbsp;
work on Guardians of the Galaxy,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:25.380 --> 00:00:29.880
The Suicide Squad, and Peacemaker. In a&nbsp;
joint statement, Gunn and Safran said:

00:00:29.880 --> 00:00:33.780
"We're honored to be the stewards of&nbsp;
these DC characters we've loved since&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:33.780 --> 00:00:37.680
we were children. [...] We're excited to&nbsp;
invigorate the theatrical experience around&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:37.680 --> 00:00:43.140
the world as we tell some of the biggest, most&nbsp;
beautiful, and grandest stories ever told."

00:00:43.140 --> 00:00:47.460
Hopefully, Gunn will be able to turn&nbsp;
around the struggling DC Extended Universe,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:47.460 --> 00:00:52.440
which appears to have been renamed the "DC&nbsp;
Universe." When Gunn posted the news to Twitter,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:52.440 --> 00:00:56.700
he was inundated with congratulations&nbsp;
from fans and celebrities alike.

00:00:56.700 --> 00:01:01.260
Fans naturally started making demands&nbsp;
almost immediately, from Justice League&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:01.260 --> 00:01:05.820
sequels to Poison Ivy and Harley Quinn&nbsp;
romances — and everything in between.

00:01:05.820 --> 00:01:11.520
But Gunn still has one foot in Marvel's door&nbsp;
even as he makes his move to DC. So how does&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:11.520 --> 00:01:16.080
the head of the MCU, Kevin Feige, feel about&nbsp;
the announcement? In an interview with The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:16.080 --> 00:01:18.780
Hollywood Reporter at the premiere&nbsp;
of Black Panther: Wakanda Forever,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:18.780 --> 00:01:22.740
Kevin Feige commented on James Gunn's&nbsp;
ascension to the head of DC Studios.

00:01:22.740 --> 00:01:27.900
Unsurprisingly, the MCU czar had nothing but&nbsp;
kind things to say about Gunn's promotion,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:27.900 --> 00:01:31.620
and he insisted he's still working&nbsp;
closely with Gunn on the MCU.

00:01:32.184 --> 00:01:35.547
"We have a wonderful thing called The Guardians&nbsp;
of the Galaxy Holiday Special coming out. We&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:35.547 --> 00:01:38.607
have a wonderful thing called Guardians&nbsp;
of the Galaxy Vol. 3 coming out in May."

00:01:38.760 --> 00:01:42.600
Feige also voiced some light-hearted&nbsp;
concern about Gunn's scheduling:

00:01:43.140 --> 00:01:46.490
"How he'll have any time to work&nbsp;
on DC until May I don't know,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:46.490 --> 00:01:50.275
but once he does have the time I'll be&nbsp;
very excited. I'll be first in line."

00:01:50.745 --> 00:01:54.420
Feige and Gunn insist that there is&nbsp;
no rivalry between the two studios,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:54.420 --> 00:01:58.680
and the two seem to be as friendly as they&nbsp;
ever were. But that hasn't stopped fans on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:58.680 --> 00:02:02.640
social media from pitting the two studio heads&nbsp;
against each other. One Twitter user wrote:

00:02:02.640 --> 00:02:08.340
"Kevin Feige accidentally creating his own arch&nbsp;
nemesis is such a beautiful comic book arc."

00:02:08.340 --> 00:02:12.540
Others commended Feige on his professionalism&nbsp;
in praising Gunn, with one tweeting:

00:02:12.540 --> 00:02:17.760
"Kevin Feige might be one of my [favorite] people&nbsp;
ever. It's so wholesome to see him unconditionally&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:17.760 --> 00:02:22.200
be a Marvel Studios alum's number one&nbsp;
fan, even if it's for a rival studio."

00:02:22.200 --> 00:02:27.120
That being said, Gunn's relationship with&nbsp;
Disney wasn't always as peachy as it is now.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:27.120 --> 00:02:31.560
Back in 2018, the company fired Gunn for&nbsp;
some old, offensive tweets that were dug&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:31.560 --> 00:02:35.520
up by conservatives angered by Gunn's&nbsp;
opposition to Donald Trump. The social&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:35.520 --> 00:02:40.140
media posts were dug up by conservative media&nbsp;
outlet The Daily Caller in response to Gunn's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:40.140 --> 00:02:45.060
outspoken criticism of the then-president.&nbsp;
The tweets in question were posted in 2008&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:45.060 --> 00:02:49.080
and 2009. Alan Horn, chair of Walt&nbsp;
Disney Studios at the time, said:

00:02:49.080 --> 00:02:54.180
"The offensive attitudes and statements discovered&nbsp;
on James' Twitter feed are indefensible and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:54.180 --> 00:02:59.040
inconsistent with our studio's values, and we&nbsp;
have severed our business relationship with him."

00:02:59.040 --> 00:03:02.460
It's worth noting that, in a 2021&nbsp;
interview with The Hollywood Reporter,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:02.460 --> 00:03:07.440
Gunn said that Horn's decision was as much of a&nbsp;
shock to Kevin Feige as it was to anybody else.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:07.440 --> 00:03:11.820
In a now-deleted tweet, Gunn responded&nbsp;
that, in the early days of his career,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:11.820 --> 00:03:16.980
he thought of himself as a "provocateur," often&nbsp;
telling jokes that were "outrageous and taboo."

00:03:16.980 --> 00:03:21.120
He also claimed to have grown as a person since&nbsp;
making those jokes. According to Deadline,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:21.120 --> 00:03:24.600
the public apology that Gunn made and&nbsp;
his contrite attitude throughout the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:24.600 --> 00:03:29.760
whole process led to Marvel rehiring Gunn.&nbsp;
Horn met with Gunn on several occasions to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:29.760 --> 00:03:33.900
discuss the incident and seemed to think that&nbsp;
the director was truly sorry for his tweets.

00:03:33.900 --> 00:03:37.380
Evidently, Gunn seems to have won&nbsp;
fans' trust over the years too,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:37.380 --> 00:03:41.820
and most people seem to be perfectly&nbsp;
happy with his new position. What his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:41.820 --> 00:03:45.120
promotion means for the DCU,&nbsp;
however, remains to be seen.

